.TH geectl-config-import-oscrc 1  "geectl-config-import-oscrc 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-config\-import\-oscrc \- Import one instance mapping from an oscrc file (one\-time migration). Reads the oscrc file once, on explicit request — geectl never reads it at runtime — and writes only the alias to apiurl mapping into the config `[instances]` table. The password is never stored and never printed: set it with the printed `GEECTL_OBS_PASSWORD_<ALIAS>` variable yourself. Dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` writes the config
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl config import\-oscrc\fR [\fB\-\-oscrc\fR] [\fB\-\-apiurl\fR] [\fB\-\-alias\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Import one instance mapping from an oscrc file (one\-time migration). Reads the oscrc file once, on explicit request — geectl never reads it at runtime — and writes only the alias to apiurl mapping into the config `[instances]` table. The password is never stored and never printed: set it with the printed `GEECTL_OBS_PASSWORD_<ALIAS>` variable yourself. Dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` writes the config
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-oscrc\fR \fI<OSCRC>\fR
The oscrc file to read (default `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/osc/oscrc`, else `~/.config/osc/oscrc`)
.TP
\fB\-\-apiurl\fR \fI<APIURL>\fR
The apiurl section to import. Required when the file holds more than one section with a username; the only such section otherwise
.TP
\fB\-\-alias\fR \fI<ALIAS>\fR
The instance alias to write. Defaults to the apiurl host with non\-alphanumerics as `_`
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Replace the alias when it already names another URL
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
